title: Authorizations › Queue › Filter by request type
route: /authorizations?type=retro
intro: The 'Request type' menu, how the demo's eight request types map onto its four choices, and how the choice travels in the web address so a link can open the queue already filtered.
dir: TD
also: Demo only: the type of each request is seed data. Peer-to-peer, Appeal and Resubmission have no choice of their own, so those requests show only under 'All request types'. The mapping is one small function (requestKindOf in src/data/queue.ts).
---
screen fb "Filter bar under the figures\nSearch, Payer, Request type, Status, Urgency"
click c1 "Click 'Request type'"
overlay m1 "Menu: All request types, Initial, Concurrent review, Reauthorization, Retrospective"
input i1 "Pick a type"

group gM "How the demo's types map"
  process k1 "**Initial**\nInitial request, Admission"
  process k2 "**Concurrent review**\nContinued stay"
  process k3 "**Reauthorization**\nRecertification"
  process k4 "**Retrospective**\nRetro-authorization"
  process k5 "**Only under All request types**\nPeer-to-peer, Appeal, Resubmission"
endgroup

process ap "The queue keeps the requests of that type\nIt stacks with search, payer, status and urgency\nThe menu turns green"
screen hd "Header: 'X of 56 open requests match these filters.'\nBand counts follow"
decision dAny "Any request left?"
screen res "Bands show the matching requests\nFor example Retrospective: R-1101 only"
screen emp "'No requests match these filters' + 'Clear filters'"
store addr "The type is written to the address\n?type=initial, concurrent, reauth or retro"
click all "Pick 'All request types' or click 'Clear filters'"
process clr "Filter off, ?type= leaves the address"

start s2 "Open a link such as /authorizations?type=retro"
decision dV "Is the value one of the four?"
process ld "The queue opens already filtered, and the menu shows the choice"
process ig "The value is ignored\nThe queue opens unfiltered, with any other filters the address names"
process oth "The same address also takes ?payer=, ?status=, ?urgency=, ?q= and ?signal=1\nValues that are not menu options are ignored"
goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › Queue › Search and filter"

fb --> c1 --> m1 --> i1
i1 --> k1 & k2 & k3 & k4 & k5
k1 --> ap
k2 --> ap
k3 --> ap
k4 --> ap
k5 -.-> ap
ap --> hd --> dAny
dAny -->|Yes| res
dAny -->|No| emp
ap --> addr
res --> all --> clr
emp --> all
s2 --> dV
dV -->|Yes| ld --> ap
dV -->|No| ig
s2 -.-> oth
fb --> g1
